No search-input code in this directory, so generic version; `/api/search`, `#search`, `render` are placeholders.

```js
const input = document.querySelector('#search');
let timer, controller;

input.addEventListener('input', () => {
  clearTimeout(timer);
  timer = setTimeout(async () => {
    controller?.abort();
    controller = new AbortController();
    try {
      const res = await fetch(`/api/search?q=${encodeURIComponent(input.value)}`, {
        signal: controller.signal,
      });
      render(await res.json());
    } catch (e) {
      if (e.name !== 'AbortError') console.error(e);
    }
  }, 300);
});
```

React equivalent:

```jsx
useEffect(() => {
  const controller = new AbortController();
  const timer = setTimeout(() => {
    fetch(`/api/search?q=${encodeURIComponent(query)}`, { signal: controller.signal })
      .then((r) => r.json())
      .then(setResults)
      .catch((e) => e.name !== 'AbortError' && console.error(e));
  }, 300);
  return () => {
    clearTimeout(timer);
    controller.abort();
  };
}, [query]);
```

Each keystroke resets the 300ms timer → one call per typing pause. Abort is not optional: debounce alone still lets a slow early response land after a newer one and overwrite the results with stale data.

